# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Arcom POS (React + Vite) — local development
# Copy to .env: cp .env.example .env
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ reach the client bundle. Everything
# else here is invisible to the app — this file is NOT a place for secrets.

# Base URL of the cloud relay (admin-panel, Next.js).
# The default baked into the code is http://localhost:3001, which matches
# `next dev -p 3001` in apps/admin-panel/package.json — so you normally
# don't need to set this for local dev. Point it at your deployed relay
# (https://api.arcom.com.ar) when building a real desktop build.
# VITE_CLOUD_API_BASE="http://localhost:3001"

# Ed25519 PUBLIC key (SPKI PEM) used to verify license tokens offline.
# Every licensed feature in the POS is gated on this signature, so a wrong
# key means the app silently refuses to validate any license.
#
# The value below is the DEV key pair, and it is also hardcoded as the
# fallback in src/lib/license.ts. Setting it here changes nothing for dev —
# it exists so the requirement is explicit instead of accidental.
#
# For production you MUST set the matching PUBLIC key here at build time,
# and it MUST correspond to the LICENSE_PRIVATE_KEY in apps/admin-panel.
# Anyone can extract this value from the shipped bundle: it is public by
# design. Only the private key is secret.
# VITE_LICENSE_PUBLIC_KEY="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\nMCowBQYDK2VwAyEAUkhabgK5W7rjvxuR3e1sa67XSieFUKXfFTPSgYzTBqQ=\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----\n"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT settable here — shell env only
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TAURI_DEV_HOST lets a physical device (phone on the same Wi-Fi) load the
# dev server instead of localhost, forwarding Vite HMR over ws://host:1421.
#
# It is read as `process.env.TAURI_DEV_HOST` in vite.config.ts, which runs
# in Node and is never populated from .env files. Export it in your shell:
#
#   TAURI_DEV_HOST=192.168.1.50 pnpm --filter pos-react dev
